 The Audit Team assessed selected controls in Happy Town, an English learning centre management web application. Original fieldwork used the loopback lab on port 3300. Playwright follow-up used the same revision on port 3302 with a copied synthetic database. The audit covered sign-in, sessions, role permissions, student and group access, validation and admin contact search.
 
-The final outcome is **11 Pass, 4 Fail and 2 Inconclusive** across 17 selected OWASP ASVS 5.0.0 Level 1 requirements. The original fieldwork recorded 11 Pass, 2 Fail and 4 Inconclusive. A later documentation review confirmed that the available application documentation did not meet the requirements for credential-abuse protection and authorization rules. The corresponding implementation cases were assessed separately. The follow-up confirmed the synthetic email in the search URL and the browser's signed-out state. Server acceptance of a prior JWT after logout remains untested. [Original execution record](../methodology/test-execution.md) · [Dated reassessment](../evidence/reassessment/2026-11-19-documentation-review.md) · [Final verification matrix](../asvs/verification-matrix.csv)
