 **Recommendation and closure.** Keep durable per-session revocation state and have the server consult it consistently, including after renewal. Use an authorized, isolated synthetic follow-up to verify that the server rejects revoked and expired sessions and that revocation persists. Corroborate with ordinary sign-out, retaining only redacted state and outcome indicators.
 
+**Related control deviation, HT-11 · ASVS v5.0.0-7.2.4 · Fail (source-based).** Successful re-authentication issues a new JWT, and the server has no decision that invalidates the superseded token. This shares the server-side revocation gap documented in HT-F01 under the distinct re-authentication trigger. Playwright verified the second login and current-session access. Acceptance or rejection of the old JWT was not observed. HT-F01 remains the registered logout finding with its original rating. The register contains four findings. [Independent source determination](../evidence/supplementary/2026-11-20/ht11-independent-source-review/HT11-fail-determination-and-proposed-changes.md).
